.TH RESOLVEPKG 1 "September 2026" "Saphira Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
resolvepkg \- dependency and package resolution planner
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B resolvepkg
.I PACKAGE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B resolvepkg
prints the
.I saphira-build-plan/v1
JSON document for building
.IR PACKAGE :
which native producers must build (with their full dependency
closure) and which artifacts satisfy from the trusted repositories.
Resolution is repository-first: a satisfying trusted APK is reused
and never rebuilt merely because a newer recipe exists; an explicit
top-level request always plans the current native recipe.
.PP
Repository immutability is enforced at plan time: an exact NVR
already published in any generation repository is never scheduled
for rebuild (the repair is
.BR promote-repo ,
never a rebuild), a recipe that would resolve from a disabled recipe
fails closed, and a known-working reference recipe without a native
producer is a porting error, not a silent skip.
.SH OPTIONS
This command takes no options beyond the package name.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /recipes
Native recipe tree (producers of last resort).
.TP
.I /reference-package-recipes/
Read-only known-working catalogue named in porting errors.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Plan printed.
.TP
.B 1
Unresolvable output, disabled producer, immutability violation, or
invalid package name.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
resolvepkg nginx | python3 -m json.tool | head -30
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR recipe (5),
.BR saphira (7),
.BR buildpkg (1),
.BR checkpkg (1),
.BR bumppkg (1),
.BR sign-apk-repo (8)
